":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":345,"closed_issues":2336,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:21:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":17,"created_at":"2026-10-10T01:37:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T13:30:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124346","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124346.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #124224\r\n\r\nWhen a Tree has sticky items, `scroll_to_item()` only accounts for the column title height. The sticky rows occupy part of the top of the control, so the target item can still end up underneath a sticky parent after scrolling.\r\n\r\n`ensure_cursor_is_visible()` already handles this correctly. This change applies the same calculation to `scroll_to_item()`:\r\n\r\n- Use `sticky_offset.y` when the target item itself is sticky.\r\n- Account for `sticky_stack_end` for regular items.\r\n- Reduce the available viewport height by the sticky stack height.\r\n\r\nThis keeps programmatic scrolling consistent with the way sticky items are drawn and clipped. No caller changes are needed.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted code\r\n﻿\r\nThe following code in scene/gui/tree.cpp was written with AI assistance:\r\n﻿\r\nTree::_ensure_cursor_is_visible(bool p_defer_vertical_scroll): Deferred vertical scrolling and cursor-visibility handling.\r\n﻿\r\nTree::_ensure_cursor_is_visible_deferred(): Rechecks cursor visibility after deferred execution.\r\n﻿\r\nAll other code changes in this PR were written by me. I reviewed and tested the changes.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124346/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124346/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}